{"cmd":["init"],"rc":0,"stdout":{"text":"hydo: created hydo/hydo.yaml\nhydo: created hydo/checks/final_todo\nhydo: created hydo/regressions/README.md\nhydo: created hydo/workload/parallel_driver_todo\nhydo: added .hydo/ to .gitignore\nhydo: added hydo/images/ to .gitignore\nhydo: AGENTS.md: hydo section created\nhydo: next: give your AI tool this instruction: \"run `hydo guide` and follow it\"\nhydo:       check the folder with: hydo build hydo/hydo.yaml --check\n"},"stderr":{"text":""},"files":[[".gitignore","644",{"text":"# hydo (hydo init): the build cache and fetched images\n.hydo/\nhydo/images/\n"}],["AGENTS.md","644",{"text":"# Instructions for coding agents\n\n<!-- hydo:begin (written by `hydo init`; edits between these markers are replaced) -->\n## Testing with hydo\n\nThis repository is tested with hydo, a deterministic hypervisor that runs the whole system under\nseeded faults and replays every failure exactly. The test lives in `hydo/`: `hydo/hydo.yaml`\n(the services and allowed faults), `hydo/workload/` (one command per client operation),\n`hydo/checks/` (the properties) and `hydo/regressions/` (saved failing schedules).\n\nBefore you change anything in `hydo/`, run `hydo guide` and follow it; `hydo guide manifest`\nexplains the project format and `hydo guide schema` prints its JSON Schema. After a change, run\n`hydo build hydo/hydo.yaml --check`; `hydo migrate` rewrites an old file in the current format.\n<!-- hydo:end -->\n"}],["home/","0",{"text":""}],["hydo/","0",{"text":""}],["hydo/checks/","0",{"text":""}],["hydo/checks/final_todo","755",{"skill":"skills/hydo-onboard/assets/hydo-init/hydo/checks/final_todo"}],["hydo/hydo.yaml","644",{"text":"# hydo plan for <CWDNAME>, written by `hydo init`. Fill in every TODO; `hydo guide` explains how,\n# `hydo guide manifest` explains the format and `hydo guide schema` prints its JSON Schema.\n# Check it with:  hydo build hydo/hydo.yaml --check\n# If the repository has a docker-compose.yaml, start from it instead (it replaces this file):\n#   hydo compose docker-compose.yaml --out hydo/hydo.yaml --images-dir images\nname: <CWDNAME>\ndescription: TODO one line about the system under test\nformat: 1                        # the project format (experimental until hydo 1.0; additions only)\nhydo_version: \"0.1\"              # the hydo this project was made for\n\nguest:\n  ram_mib: 1024                  # must hold every service (256..3072 on x86_64, 256..4096 on arm64)\n  # cpu: v3                      # x86_64 only: AVX/AVX2 for binaries built for x86-64-v3\n  # clock_after_cut: 60          # when a check compares times from before and after a power cut\n\nroot:\n  files: []                      # TODO the binaries and config files: {src: <relative to this file>, dst: /bin/x, mode: \"0755\"}\n\ndata:\n  size_mib: 512                  # the persistent data disk, mounted on /data (the fault target)\n  dirs: []                       # TODO the services' data directories, created under /data\n\nservices: []                     # TODO one entry per long-running process (name, cmd, ready, port, ...)\n\nworkload:\n  steps: 20                      # rounds of the composition; faults are placed at round numbers\n  timeout: 300\n\ntest:                            # the test composer: hydo/workload/ holds the commands, hydo/checks/ the checks\n  parallel: 4                    # at most this many commands at once\n  per_round: 2                   # parallel drivers started per round\n  round_ms: 200                  # a round every 200 ms of guest time\n\nfaults: [kill, pause, network, oneway, cut, clock, disk]   # TODO keep the kinds that make sense\n"}],["hydo/regressions/","0",{"text":""}],["hydo/regressions/README.md","644",{"skill":"skills/hydo-onboard/assets/hydo-init/hydo/regressions/README.md"}],["hydo/workload/","0",{"text":""}],["hydo/workload/parallel_driver_todo","755",{"skill":"skills/hydo-onboard/assets/hydo-init/hydo/workload/parallel_driver_todo"}]],"setup":"nothing","id":"18.0"}
